---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { enterprise, site } from '../content/site';

// Separate planned enterprise capabilities from the available MIT core.
const agents = ['Claude Code', 'Copilot', 'Cursor', 'Codex'];
const sources = ['GitHub', 'GitLab', 'Jira', 'Slack'];
const pillars = [
  {
    title: 'Recall respects access',
    body: 'Planned source-aware permissions: a memory learned in a private repository should only reach developers who can open that repository.',
    status: 'planned',
  },
  {
    title: 'Leads approve what spreads',
    body: 'Planned promotion policy: a lesson can spread from a repository to a team or company within the administrator’s configured approval rules.',
    status: 'planned',
  },
  {
    title: 'Every write is on the record',
    body: 'The MIT core records supported operations in an audit log and provides tenant-scoped API keys, admin/member roles and per-key scope grants.',
    status: 'available in MIT core',
  },
];
const kpis = [
  { name: 'Cost per merged PR', how: 'from your agent’s own billing telemetry' },
  { name: 'Read tokens per session', how: 'the share spent re-reading files' },
  { name: 'Repeat-error rate', how: 'the same failure seen again in a later session' },
  { name: 'Guardrails', how: 'reverts, rejected reviews and CI failures must not rise' },
];
---

<Base
  title="hippo for teams: memory your platform team can approve"
  description="The commercial edition of hippo is planned and its private repository is a scaffold. Ask about a scoped pilot for governed shared memory inside your network."
  crumb="Teams"
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 hero-glow"></div>
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-5 pb-(--section-y) pt-10 sm:pt-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-acc-amber/40 bg-acc-amber/10 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-acc-amber">
            {enterprise.status} · pilot requests open
          </span>
          <h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-[1.1] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
            The memory layer your <span class="text-gradient">platform team</span> can approve.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            {enterprise.availability} The goal is governed shared memory inside your network, with source-aware access and routine capture after initial setup and required trust. Agent-by-agent automatic-save coverage and enterprise acceptance are still planned.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href={site.links.pilot} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-xl bg-acc-violet px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-950 transition hover:opacity-90">Ask about a pilot</a>
            <a href={site.links.security} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-xl border border-white/12 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-200 transition hover:bg-white/5">Security policy</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass min-w-0 rounded-2xl p-6" aria-label="Planned enterprise deployment">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400">Planned enterprise deployment</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-4">
            {agents.map((a) => <li class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 px-3 py-2.5 text-center text-sm text-zinc-200">{a}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-center font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">Planned: MCP over OAuth, signed in as the developer</p>
          <div class="mt-3 rounded-xl border-2 border-dashed border-acc-violet/50 p-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-acc-violet">YOUR NETWORK</p>
            <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-lg bg-zinc-900 px-4 py-3">
              <span class="font-display text-base">hippo server</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">Postgres · Helm · SSO · audit log</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-4">
              {sources.map((s) => <li class="rounded-md bg-white/[0.04] px-2 py-2 text-center text-sm text-zinc-300">{s}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-400">Available today: the MIT core, the HTTP server with tenants, API keys and an audit log, and GitHub and Slack connectors. Postgres, Helm, SSO and additional enterprise sources are planned; this diagram is not a released deployment bundle.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/5">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-4 px-5 py-(--section-y) md:grid-cols-3">
        {pillars.map((p) => (
          <div class="glass flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <span class:list={['self-start rounded px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs', p.status === 'available in MIT core' ? 'bg-acc-violet/15 text-acc-violet' : 'bg-acc-amber/15 text-acc-amber']}>{p.status}</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl leading-snug">{p.title}</h2>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">{p.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02]">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-(--section-y) lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-acc-violet">Proposed pilot</p>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Measured on your work, against a holdout.</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
            Agree the scope, duration, customer outcomes and quality guardrails before the pilot. Compare against a holdout that cannot receive shared lessons from the treatment group, using comparable people, tasks, days and models. Join permitted agent telemetry and independently accepted outcomes inside your network; include setup, supervision and administrator effort.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-sm text-zinc-400">Reporting and automated joins are planned commercial work. Missing outcomes stay unknown, and the proposed report must show a null or negative result as clearly as a gain. We publish our own losses too.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="glass min-w-0 divide-y divide-white/8 rounded-2xl">
          {kpis.map((k) => (
            <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 px-6 py-4">
              <span class="font-display text-base">{k.name}</span>
              <span class="text-sm text-zinc-400">{k.how}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
          <li class="px-6 py-4 font-mono text-sm text-acc-violet">with hippo vs holdout · 95% interval · your result</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
